{{Short description|Football tournament}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
Play in Group C of the [[2006 FIFA World Cup]] began on 10 June 2006 and ended on 21 June. [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] won the group and advanced to the round of 16, along with the [[Netherlands national football team|Netherlands]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Saaid |first=Hamdan |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/2006full.html |title=World Cup 2006 – Match Details |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |date=7 February 2007 |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The two sides tied on points in the standings, but Argentina won the tie-break on goal difference and ended the group in first with the Netherlands in second place. The [[Ivory Coast national football team|Ivory Coast]] and [[Serbia and Montenegro national football team|Serbia and Montenegro]] failed to advance.

Upon completion of the draw for the tournament, many football pundits remarked that this group appeared to be the "[[group of death]]", despite the fact that only Argentina had qualified for the [[2002 FIFA World Cup|previous World Cup]].

